questions.stem:
A turnstile tester sums taps with this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("4 7 2");
int t = 0;
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { t += sc.nextInt(); }
System.out.println(t);
What value is printed?

A nursery counts saplings listed one per line with this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("elm\noak\npine");
int n = 0;
while (sc.hasNextLine()) { sc.nextLine(); n++; }
System.out.println(n);
What value is printed?

A bakery inventory reads nothing from its file with this line:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("data.txt");
Which statement identifies the fault?

A swim club totals one results row with this fragment:
String line = "mia,82,91";
String[] parts = line.split(",");
int total = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]) + Integer.parseInt(parts[2]);
System.out.println(total);
What value is printed?

A market report starts with a title row that must be skipped:
Scanner sc = new Scanner(new File("sales.csv"));
_____;
while (sc.hasNextLine()) { process(sc.nextLine()); }
Which line belongs in the blank?

A farm stand parses price rows like "pear,2.49" with this fragment:
String[] p = line.split(",");
double price = _____;
Which fragment belongs in the blank?

A dock scanner tracks the heaviest crate with this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("12 27 19 33 21");
int best = sc.nextInt();
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { int x = sc.nextInt(); if (x > best) { best = x; } }
System.out.println(best);
What integer is printed?

A ticket gate never recognizes the quit code with this test:
String code = sc.nextLine();
if (code == "quit") { break; }
Which statement identifies the fault?

A timing crew tracks the fastest lap from a number stream:
int best = sc.nextInt();
int n = 1;
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { int x = sc.nextInt(); n++; _____; }
Which line keeps best correct?

A donation jar mixes coins with a note word in this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("10 20 stop 30");
int t = 0;
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { t += sc.nextInt(); }
System.out.println(t);
What value is printed?

An archive tool crashes on its final read:
sc.close();
String s = sc.nextLine();
Which statement identifies the fault?

A track analyst averages lap counts read from a file:
int sum = 0, n = 0;
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { sum += sc.nextInt(); n++; }
double avg = _____;
Which fragment finishes the average?
